Description: Declare two requirements the archives can satisfy
 Neither change alters what the fork does, and neither changes the binary
 package's dependencies -- dh_python3 drops PEP 440 version constraints when
 it turns install_requires into ${python3:Depends}, so what it generates is
 the same unversioned list either way (measured on platformio, the same
 packaging, 2026-11-05). What they change is the requirement metadata the
 installed package carries, in PKG-INFO's Requires-Dist and the egg-info's
 requires.txt, where upstream's pins would have the package declare
 requirements the system it is installed on cannot satisfy. "pip check"
 reports those, and pkg_resources.require("pioarduino") raises
 VersionConflict on them.
 .
 bottle: upstream pins "== 0.13.*". noble ships 0.12.25, and the only use of
 bottle is the bottle.template() call in
 platformio/project/integration/generator.py, which is the same in 0.12 and
 0.13 -- so the pin becomes ">= 0.12".
 .
 starlette: the fork pins "< 1" and stonking ships 1.7.0, so on that series
 the pin excludes the only version there is. The fork's starlette-facing code
 is identical to upstream platformio 6.2.0 -- the same seven imports from
 starlette.applications, .middleware, .responses, .routing, .staticfiles,
 .status and .endpoints -- and upstream declares "< 2" and is built against
 stonking's 1.7.0 in this same registry. So "< 2" here, which covers noble's
 0.31.1, resolute's 0.50.0 and stonking's 1.7.0 alike.
 .
 Upstream has since raised the floor instead: pioarduino 6.2.0.post1 declares
 "starlette >=1.3.1, <2", which noble and resolute cannot meet at all. That
 is why this package stays on 6.2.0; see README.md.
